#%PAM-1.0
# Script function and purpose: PAM policy for Sakura's automatic login on
# FreeBSD. It permits authentication without a password, then defers account,
# password and session handling to the system login stack.

# pam_permit.so replaces the base system's entire auth stack rather than adding
# to it, so everything that stack would have enforced is bypassed -- that being
# the point of automatic login, but worth stating plainly: this policy
# authenticates nobody.
#
# The other three facilities still defer to the system login stack, which is
# what keeps the session itself identical to a normal login. In particular
# `session include login` reaches /etc/pam.d/system and so runs pam_xdg(8),
# which creates /var/run/xdg/$USER and publishes XDG_RUNTIME_DIR. A Wayland
# compositor cannot create its socket without it, so dropping that line would
# break a graphical autologin specifically.
#
# Nothing here needs the leading "-" (non-fatal module) prefix, which OpenPAM
# only understands from FreeBSD 15.0. Since 15.0 is the baseline it is
# available if a future addition wants it. The Linux policy stays a separate
# file because it names distribution-specific modules with no FreeBSD
# counterpart.
auth       required     pam_permit.so
account    include      login
password   include      login
session    include      login
